Exp34 frozen — Track B medium-term structural location -> next-day directional continuation. Use completed M5 broker-days strictly before 2026-08-13 00:00 BRT and drop first/last file-edge broker-days. For each completed day t define RollingHigh20_t=max(High over t-19..t), RollingLow20_t=min(Low over t-19..t), Position20_t=(Close_t-RollingLow20_t)/(RollingHigh20_t-RollingLow20_t) when denominator>0, and day_sign_t=sign(Close_t-Open_t). For target day d define PrevAlignedPosition20_d = day_sign_{d-1} * (2*Position20_{d-1}-1), so +1 means the prior close sat at the 20-day extreme aligned with the prior day's direction and -1 means opposite. Target y_continue_d=1 iff day_sign_d==day_sign_{d-1}. Eligible target days require current and prior non-zero sign and valid prior 20-day position. PrevAlignedPosition20Centered = feature - TRAIN mean, frozen before OOS. Split whole eligible ISO weeks chronologically 60/20/20; no week may straddle splits. BASE is TRAIN constant P(y_continue=1). EXTENDED freezes BASE and fits exactly one TRAIN coefficient k_location on the continuous centered feature. Primary unit=completed broker-day; primary estimand=DAY_WEIGHTED; uncertainty=resamples whole ISO broker-weeks preserving day weights. Survival requires Brier and LogLoss gain CI95>0 in BOTH Validation and TEST.

Exp34 anti-rescue contract: exact 20 completed-day high/low window only; no 10/30/60 alternatives, thresholds, bins, quantiles, distance-to-high/low decomposition, raw unsigned Position20, UP/DOWN coefficient split, streak/efficiency/compression interaction, weekday/D1/Clock/Z/Fib/Track-D context, or alternate target after result. If Exp34 fails, close this exact medium-term aligned-location -> next-day continuation hypothesis and pause simple first-order Track-B feature search for a methodological checkpoint before opening another family. Historical OOS remains exploratory. Exp27 untouched. Runtime promotion NONE.